# Phase 1: HTTP Client Replacement - Implementation Summary

## Overview

This document summarizes the completion of **Phase 1** of the Akka dependency removal from OBP-API. Phase 1 focused on replacing the HTTP client functionality while maintaining full backward compatibility.

## What Was Accomplished

### 1. New HTTP Client Implementation

**File:** `OBP-API/obp-api/src/main/scala/code/util/StandardHttpClient.scala`

- ✅ Created a new HTTP client using Apache HttpClient
- ✅ Implements connection pooling (max 200 connections, 20 per route)
- ✅ Configurable timeouts and retry logic (3 attempts)
- ✅ Asynchronous operation using Scala Futures
- ✅ Comprehensive error handling and logging

**Key Features:**
- Connection pool management with idle connection cleanup
- HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2.0 support
- JSON content type handling
- Proper resource cleanup
- Performance optimizations

### 2. Backward-Compatible AkkaHttpClient Replacement

**File:** `OBP-API/obp-api/src/main/scala/code/util/AkkaHttpClient.scala` (Updated)

- ✅ Maintains identical API interface to original AkkaHttpClient
- ✅ Internally delegates to StandardHttpClient
- ✅ Preserves all existing method signatures
- ✅ Handles Akka HTTP types (HttpRequest, HttpResponse, HttpMethod, etc.)
- ✅ Zero breaking changes for existing code

**Migration Strategy:**
- Existing code continues to work without modification
- Logs migration notice to encourage future migration to StandardHttpClient
- Transparent conversion between Akka HTTP and Apache HTTP types

### 3. Alternative Implementation

**File:** `OBP-API/obp-api/src/main/scala/code/util/AkkaHttpClientCompat.scala`

- ✅ Complete standalone replacement implementation
- ✅ Can be used as a future reference or alternative approach

### 4. Deprecation Warnings

**File:** `OBP-API/obp-api/src/main/scala/code/bankconnectors/Connector.scala`

- ✅ Added deprecation warning for `akka_vDec2018` connector
- ✅ Directs users to migration documentation

## Technical Details

### HTTP Client Architecture

```
Before (Phase 1):
┌─────────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐
│   Existing Code │ -> │ AkkaHttpClient│ -> │ Akka HTTP Core  │
└─────────────────┘    └──────────────┘    └─────────────────┘

After (Phase 1):
┌─────────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐    ┌─────────────────┐
│   Existing Code │ -> │ AkkaHttpClient│ -> │StandardHttpClient│ -> │Apache HttpClient│
└─────────────────┘    └──────────────┘    └──────────────────┘    └─────────────────┘
```

### Dependencies Impact

- ✅ **No changes to Maven/SBT dependencies** - Akka HTTP still included for compatibility
- ✅ **No breaking changes** - All existing code continues to work
- ✅ **Added Apache HttpClient dependency** - Already present in project
- ✅ **Reduced runtime Akka usage** - HTTP operations now use Apache HttpClient

### Performance Improvements

| Aspect | Before | After |
|--------|--------|-------|
| Connection Pooling | Akka HTTP pools | Apache HttpClient pools (more mature) |
